-**Theorem.** Assume problem 3: omni sources, \(G\in\mathbb{A}\), \(R_{\mathrm{eff}}\ge 1000\), \(N\in[10,16]\), and the covering loop **terminates in one of the first three exit sets** (empty continuum residual, no silent channels, or 16 distinct hearings). Then the p1_sprint searcher has heard every source.
-
-This is a normal-termination correctness guarantee, not 确保全部清除, and not a proof that the covering tour finishes in finitely many steps. `MAX_ACTIONS=900` is an algorithm cap, not a number from the official problem PDF. Real-time window, process runtime, and technical exceptions are additional residuals.
-
-Proof. Suppose some source \(G\) is never heard and the loop nevertheless ended in one of the first three sets. Then every silent-channel measurement (hence every discovery station) satisfies \(\|G-S\|>R_{\mathrm{eff}}\ge 1000\), so \(G\in\mathrm{Res}_{\mathrm{cont}}(\mathcal{S})\) at every moment. Lemma 1 puts \(G\) in some \(K_Q\). Lemma 2–3 keep that \(Q\) (or a covering waypoint of \(K_Q\)) as a covering goal until a silent scan covers \(K_Q\), which would hear \(G\). Empty residual, empty silent set, and 16 distinct hearings each contradict an unheard leftover source. Contradiction.
-
----
-
-## 7. The old hole is closed
-
-Sprint `_residual_samples` tested a finite \(W=\) `q3_residual_witnesses()`. Empty \(W\)-residual is not empty continuum residual. \(G_\star\) at \(7.5^\circ\) sits in a leftover component with no point of \(W\); neighbouring \(15^\circ\) witnesses were covered, \(R_0\) was pruned, channel 20 was never heard.
-
-This code does not consult \(W\) for prune, fallback, covering-goal emptiness, or silent-scan filtering. After the seven-station set of sprint `detection_proof.md` §4, `scout_meets_residual(R_0, S)` is true and \(\rho(\mathcal{S},\mathbb{A})>1000\). On the TwinClient instance of that write-up (\(N=11\), channel 20 at \(G_\star\), \(R_{\mathrm{eff}}=1000\)), the p1 searcher hears and clears all 11 sources, including channel 20.
-
-That run is a check that the hole is gone, not an independent covering theorem.
-
----
-
-## 8. What is not claimed
-
-- **Clearance** (\(20\,\mathrm{m}\) disk, LOB homing) is a separate certificate. This theorem is detection under normal termination: the radio is heard. It does not prove 确保全部清除, and it does not prove the covering loop must finish in finitely many steps.
-- **Time.** Covering waypoints, D-opt, and savings-rule inserts are heuristics for virtual time. A failed heuristic falls back to the remaining 9-net (Lemma 1) then one service TSP. After origin is a discovery station, the first point of each segment \(O\to R_k\) that continuum-covers \(K_{R_k}\) is \(R_k\) itself (\(t=1\)). Origin-heard \(G\) (those with \(\|G\|\le 1000\)) leave 8 ring cells almost intact. Those facts are why a cheaper covering city does not delete the ring obligation; they are not the detection theorem.
-- **Monte Carlo cover fractions** and 演练 full-clear rates are not this proof.
-- **Float.** Lemma 3 is geometric. The implementation uses float64 circumcentres and a \(10^{-6}\,\mathrm{m}\) expansion of \(K\). Skip is conservative under a raised \(\rho\). A missed nearly-collinear circumcentre lies far outside \(\mathbb{A}\) and is not the leftover of \(K\); leftover on \(\partial K\) is enumerated by bisector–circle intersections.
-
